comjohn@ccu1.aukuni.ac.nz (Mr. John T Jensen) writes:
: 
: My 12-year old has asked me to post three questions about PC nethack (sorry,
: don't know what version he has):
: 
: 1)      He has found half a dozen or so throne rooms, killed all the
: 	monsters, and sits on the throne.  When he does, he is told
: 	"you feel out of place" and the throne disappears.  Has anyone
: 	any comment?
:
Well, all sorts of things can happen.  I forget exactly what the chances
are based on...  It's a good idea to drop all your gold before sitting,
because it might all disappear.  On the brighter side, you might be granted
a wish!  It's generally worth the risk.
 
: 2)	He knows how to get Excalibur, but wants to know how to get:
: 
: -	a katana named Snickersnee
: -	a war hammer named Mjollnir
: -	a broadsword named Stormbringer
: 
The trick is to offer corpses at an altar of your alignment.  You may
eventually be granted an artifact, other nice things can happen too.
Of course you could wish for them, or be unbelievably lucky and find them
lying around.

: 3)	The verb 'pray' does not give a syntax error, but 'offer' does.
: 	There are altars.  Any suggestions?
: 
Offer is an extended command, and is thus rather specialized.  One uses it
to offer corpses to one's deity at the appropriate altar.  The command to
type is "#o".  Pray is handy for getting out of all sorts of scrapes,
provided the gods like you.

